Finally made it.  Not a very interesting story, but I'll tell it.

Found a bones file on level 5 with a coaligned altar: one of my old
wizards carrying a blessed  +2 SDSM, uncursed burnt +0 cloak of magic
resistance, uncursed Magicbane, cursed sack, and some cursed rings (one
later turns out to be levitation, I think another is free action).
Thus I am possibly the first Valkyrie EVER to get Magicbane as her
first artifact weapon.

I continue down to the Oracle on level 7 and start dipping my long
sword in her fountains (is there a risk I could drown her or piss her
off if they flood?).  The first fountain disappears and leaves me with
a bunch of water moccasins, which might have killed me if I didn't have
Magicbane to engrave Elbereth.  Good deal.  The second one doesn't work
either.  No Excalibur, only some crappy water demon offering me a wish.
 I guess that'll have to do.

I look around at my situation: I haven't gone through Sokoban yet, so I
don't want to blow a wish on a bag of holding, but I already have MC3,
MR, and reflection.  It's either gauntlets of power or speed boots; I
wish for gauntlets of power because of the coaligned altar.  I figure
I'll soon be getting Mjollnir, and I love throwing Mjollnir.  Just such
a cool image.  It's not good enough to have an electric war hammer, it
has to be one that you can throw and it will come back to you.  This
was one of my dumbest mistakes of the whole game, though it was a small
one.  I should know by now: never wish for gauntlets of power if you
need speed boots, because gauntlets of power are EVERYWHERE.  I later
found four pairs in the main dungeon before Gehennom ALONE; the only
randomly generated speed boots I ever ran across were halfway down in
Gehennom.

Oh well.  The third fountain gives me Excalibur.  I run through the
gnomish mines, finding the Minetown altar to be coaligned.  I sell a
couple identified gems for some cash, which gives me a nice AC boost.
My pet dies soon after this.  The Wine Cellar at the end of the mines
gets me my luckstone (which I immediately bless; no lack of holy water
here!) and a bunch of gems that I can't even carry because I don't have
a bag of holding.  I can't carry half of the good stuff I've found at
this point.  I begin to realize how much it sucks not to have a bag of
holding.  I go back up and start zapping wands of create monster in the
Minetown temple.  For all my trouble I don't get Mjollnir, but I do
catch the priestess in an explosion from a gas spore or whatever
they're called.  Now she's angry.  Fortunately I had locked the door,
so I just zap a wand of digging down and let her stay in there.  I
continue the sacrificing back at the other altar, and get Mjollnir.  I
proceed to leave Mjollnir in a box somewhere because it's too heavy to
carry and will blow up wands and rings.

Sokoban has an amulet of reflection; I just leave it there and remember
what it looks like.  I'm only level 11 or 12, so I go down all the way
to Medusa's Island instead of going on the quest.  On the way I find a
ring of teleport control, a magic marker, and some other goodies; I eat
a tengu or something to get teleportitis.  I get to Medusa's Island and
realize that, unlike in most of my recent games, I don't have an amulet
of magical breathing on me, and thus I actually have to worry about
krakens for probably the first time ever.  Not cool.  I dig down to the
next level, which is the castle, and come back up the stairs.  This is
the stupidest mistake I made all game, because I forgot to blindfold
myself first.  Only the speed system saved me, and I don't think I was
even fast, let alone very fast!  I quickly blindfold myself and Medusa
kills herself thanks to reflection.  Around this time I hit level 14,
so I go back up and clear the quest.  Somewhere along the line I find
two uncursed scrolls.  I read one and it turns out to be genocide.  I
genocide mind flayers, because I can't really think of a better option,
then I bless the other scroll and wipe out all ;  .   Problem solved.

The castle was uneventful; wand was (0:2).  I get speed boots, an extra
magic marker, a bag of holding, an amulet of life saving, and a ring of
polymorph control (I already have a cursed ring of polymorph), and save
the last wish for later.  After this everything is pretty
straightforward, not much to say.  Found another wand of wishing in
Gehennom (where was that in the early game when I needed it?)  I try
wishing for a blessed figurine of a purple worm, but it hits a
polymorph trap and turns into a dingo soon after.  Thanks for nothing.

The Vibrating Square was on level 44; everything went pretty smoothly.
By this point I had two wands of death and enough magic marker charges
for lots of scrolls of charging, so killing the Wizard and keeping him
dead was no problem.  Moloch's Sanctum was more annoying than
dangerous; my biggest problem was switching back and forth between
Magicbane (to avoid having my stuff cursed) and Excalibur (level drain
resistance for the vampires).  Getting in was tough; getting out with
the Amulet was easy, as I just ran straight through all the fire traps
and nothing got in my way.  My trip up wasn't too bad; most of the
stairs were close together and I didn't get sent back more than a
couple times.  Magicbane kept almost all my items from being cursed,
and I was more than well enough equipped to uncurse the one or two that
had problems.  The Wizard reappeared four times counting the Plane of
Earth; my wands of death nailed him each time before he could cause
trouble.  The Planes were easy.  Death was in the middle, so I went
right (the nearest altar to me) and zapped Pestilence with a wand of
death.  The altar there was chaotic, so I wished for a helm of opposite
alignment and ascended.

